From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:55:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 135/139] dt-bindings: usb: qcom,snps-dwc3: Add mode-switch

The QMP USB3-DP combo PHY stops the USB3 PIPE clock when a Type-C
DisplayPort pin assignment gives it all four lanes. The controller has
to switch to the UTMI clock before that happens, so it needs the Type-C
mux state as well. Allow the controller node to be a mode switch in the
connector graph.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/qcom,snps-dwc3.yaml | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/qcom,snps-dwc3.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/qcom,snps-dwc3.yaml
index ea60f7220..bd7bf381a 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/qcom,snps-dwc3.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/qcom,snps-dwc3.yaml
@@ -155,6 +155,13 @@ properties:
       HS/FS/LS modes are supported.
     type: boolean
 
+  mode-switch:
+    description:
+      The controller receives the Type-C mux state, so that it can stop
+      depending on the USB3 PIPE clock while the combo PHY drives all
+      lanes for DisplayPort.
+    type: boolean
+
   wakeup-source: true
 
 required:
-- 
2.47.3

